{"id":"1b69d3256f9eea981c00d475","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/30/nepal-tibet-floods-missing-australians-secret-harbour-byelection-wa-tanya-plibersek-insiders-pacific-islands-forum-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-08-30T01:26:22Z","collected_at":"2026-08-30T01:45:22.346517Z","title":"News live: limits on smartglasses being considered, Plibersek says; missing Australian woman located safely in Nepal","text":"20.02 EDT Cabinet never discussed cutting refugee intake, says Plibersek Tanya Plibersek has said cabinet never discussed cutting Australia’s refugee intake after debate and confusion within Labor came into public view this week. The Financial Review on Thursday reported the home affairs minister, Tony Burke, was planning to cut intake of 20,000 arrivals to 13,750 in 2027-28. The prime minister declared the figure would stay at 20,000 after Labor MPs and refugee advocates reacted angrily. Asked on the ABC’s Insiders if the government had considered a cut to the refugee intake, Plibersek said: No, I don’t really know where this story came from. We reconfirmed our number as recently as a month ago at the national conference. There was certainly no discussion in cabinet. She said the 20,000-a-year figure was a “permanent commitment”. The party’s most recent national conference voted to approve a statement that read: Labor will seek, in the short term, to maintain Australia’s government funded humanitarian intake numbers at 20,000 places per year while also continuing to aspire to achieving 27,000 places per year.","html":"","media":[],"author":"Luca Ittimani","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"8a445800d1d1a2741a940bf2c7064a3420d6e5647b79d772fe2474e0bb8c189c","original_text_chars":1127,"original_html_chars":2142,"text_truncated":false,"media_count":0,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/30/nepal-tibet-floods-missing-australians-secret-harbour-byelection-wa-tanya-plibersek-insiders-pacific-islands-forum-ntwnfb","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/30/nepal-tibet-floods-missing-australians-secret-harbour-byelection-wa-tanya-plibersek-insiders-pacific-islands-forum-ntwnfb"}}}
{"id":"f29e0156e638792dbed44657","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/families-balance-hope-and-despair-in-race-to-find-survivors-in-nepal-as-australians-still-missing","published_at":"2026-08-30T00:27:59Z","collected_at":"2026-08-30T01:45:23.209007Z","title":"Families balance hope and despair in race to find survivors in Nepal as 41 Australians still missing","text":"Relatives of people missing following flooding in Nepal visit Tribhuvan University teaching hospital in Kathmandu, as they search for their loved ones. Photograph: Ghanashyam Shrestha/JNA/ZUMA Press Wire/Shutterstock View image in fullscreen Relatives of people missing following flooding in Nepal visit Tribhuvan University teaching hospital in Kathmandu, as they search for their loved ones. Photograph: Ghanashyam Shrestha/JNA/ZUMA Press Wire/Shutterstock Nepal-Tibet flood disaster Families balance hope and despair in race to find survivors in Nepal as 41 Australians still missing The walls of a teaching hospital are filled with pictures of unidentified victims as authorities collect DNA samples and plan burials before morgues fill up Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates Get our breaking news email , free app or daily news podcast Cait Kelly in Kathmandu Sat 29 Aug 2026 20.27 EDT Last modified on Sat 29 Aug 2026 21.38 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google S ome of them are young, some old; most of them appear to be men. Some of them could be sleeping, except for the mud that covers their bodies. Some, it seems, would be impossible to recognise even if you knew th","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/85c08f12aca94cf3bba4c613b643f7b91766f442/458_0_4582_3665/master/4582.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/uploads/2022/03/03/Cait_Kelly.png?width=75&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/159694de7a3a36b5614e9ee1b778d2820487e325/0_0_4229_2820/master/4229.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/5c3d2c0b70f31a16ccec72cea1275ceee0e75332/0_0_5000_4000/master/5000.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://media.guim.co.uk/65e9e559dcb8d01d4988a878bab77acc54462b24/0_0_3000_3000/500.jpg","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/7c38cab6e5482d8bbe0e5f55a3b7d109d5b0d6d3/0_263_1276_1021/master/1276.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Cait Kelly in Kathmandu","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"82da94e0ce7064c88b64b04cab9870ccaf9d73a4880a4e9a9cb5b4f32bb09a34","original_text_chars":9927,"original_html_chars":34798,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":6,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/families-balance-hope-and-despair-in-race-to-find-survivors-in-nepal-as-australians-still-missing","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/30/families-balance-hope-and-despair-in-race-to-find-survivors-in-nepal-as-australians-still-missing"}}}
{"id":"f8a34a20ac5612fcd5eff58b","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nation-claims-victory-on-secret-harbour-byelection-in-western-australia","published_at":"2026-08-30T00:00:28Z","collected_at":"2026-08-30T01:45:24.400144Z","title":"One Nation claims victory in Secret Harbour byelection in Western Australia","text":"One Nation candidate Luke Herdegen, seen at the Coastal Lakes college polling place in Perth on Saturday, has claimed victory in the Secret Habour byelection. Photograph: Richard Wainwright/AAP View image in fullscreen One Nation candidate Luke Herdegen, seen at the Coastal Lakes college polling place in Perth on Saturday, has claimed victory in the Secret Habour byelection. Photograph: Richard Wainwright/AAP Australia news One Nation claims victory in Secret Harbour byelection in Western Australia One Nation candidate Luke Herdegen secures 57% of the vote after preferences as Barnaby Joyce says ‘politics has changed’ Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates Get our breaking news email , free app or daily news podcast Krishani Dhanji Sat 29 Aug 2026 20.00 EDT First published on Sat 29 Aug 2026 18.29 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google Barnaby Joyce has declared “politics has changed” after One Nation claimed victory in the Secret Harbour state byelection in Western Australia . The One Nation MP celebrated the win on Sunday and said the results showed his party could convert high polling into on-the-ground votes. “I think one of the takeaways from that is our actua","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/3e3cf0448660f5e084369101cb80369f69c1e465/0_0_6563_5253/master/6563.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Krishani Dhanji","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"96e96e04229ed8818d37007a00f824a750e7e809eeba454fa08a50c249b0a71a","original_text_chars":5498,"original_html_chars":20978,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":1,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nation-claims-victory-on-secret-harbour-byelection-in-western-australia","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/30/one-nation-claims-victory-on-secret-harbour-byelection-in-western-australia"}}}
{"id":"c80e1eb7db7e10cba0928610","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-chinese-rescue-team-finds-nothing-but-ruins-after-reaching-border-crossing-hit-by-deadly-flood","published_at":"2026-08-30T01:25:41Z","collected_at":"2026-08-30T01:45:31.986031Z","title":"Number of missing in Nepal and Tibet rises to 3,000 as bad weather hampers search","text":"Chinese crews conduct search and rescue operations in Gyirong, Tibet. Photograph: China News Service/Getty View image in fullscreen Chinese crews conduct search and rescue operations in Gyirong, Tibet. Photograph: China News Service/Getty Nepal-Tibet flood disaster Number of missing in Nepal and Tibet rises to 3,000 as bad weather hampers search Nepal requests foreign ⁠help in identification and storing of bodies, DNA testing and rescuing people from tunnels Visual guide: how the deadly flooding unfolded Nepal-Tibet flash flood – latest updates Donna Ferguson and agencies Sat 29 Aug 2026 21.25 EDT First published on Fri 28 Aug 2026 22.49 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google Poor weather temporarily hampered aerial rescue operations in Nepal on Saturday as the search for thousands of missing people in areas devastated by catastrophic flash floods along the border with China continued. The combined toll in Nepal and Tibet rose to 691 dead and more than 3,000 people missing after China’s latest update on Sunday. Chinese authorities reported 16 deaths and 546 missing, while Nepal’s disaster agency said late Saturday that the death toll had climbed to 675 with 2,498 people missing. ‘","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/271a7f98e98406fa97e3618ad92eadccf60c69b2/0_0_8256_5504/master/8256.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/d05b333d817d7773aa4f805ad2d6681627055125/0_0_1920_1080/1920.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/b56b8e526066fdfd600372cdcee